                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is realistic launch budget for skincare D2C in India?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 15-25L Boutique (30-80 SKUs single-sub-category). Rs 40-60L Mid-market (80-200 SKUs, 2-3 sub-categories). Rs 90L-1.5 Cr Full-range premium (200-500 SKUs, regional multi-language).</p>
                                        <h3>What is the equivalent in AED for Dubai + UAE launch?</h3>
                                        <p>AED 90-170K Boutique + AED 230-360K Mid-market + AED 500K+ Full-range premium. Add trilingual creative + Ramadan + DSF calendar + Snapchat + ESMA + halal cost for UAE-specific.</p>
                                        <h3>What is Saudi Arabia launch budget in SAR?</h3>
                                        <p>SAR 85-160K Boutique + SAR 220-340K Mid-market + SAR 480K+ Full-range premium. Add Snapchat creative + native Arabic + Vision 2030 positioning + Umrah + Hajj + SFDA cost.</p>
                                        <h3>What is standard budget allocation for skincare launch?</h3>
                                        <p>Inventory 30-45% + Brand 12-18% + Shopify 8-14% + Photography 3-6% + Compliance 4-8% + First 6mo marketing 25-35% + Contingency 6-12%. Deviations cause common failures.</p>
                                        <h3>What is most common Rs 25L launch mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Under-invested branding (below 12%) + over-invested inventory or paid media (above 45%). Weak brand identity + packaging limits marketing effectiveness + compresses brand-search + repeat over 12-24 months.</p>
                                        <h3>How much for first 6 months marketing + ad spend?</h3>
                                        <p>25-35% of launch budget. Rs 5-8L Boutique + Rs 12-18L Mid-market + Rs 25-45L Full-range premium. Split into creative production + platform ad spend + creator + PR + content.</p>
                                        <h3>Do we need a contingency reserve?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes 6-12%. Covers unexpected inventory reorder + ad-spend surge + compliance fee + platform ban + supply chain delay. Skincare launches without contingency stall at first surprise.</p>
